Pi extensions receive an `ExtensionAPI` and register an LLM-callable tool with `pi.registerTool(...)`:

```ts
pi.registerTool<TParams extends TSchema = TSchema, TDetails = unknown, TState = any>({
  name: string,
  label: string,
  description: string,
  parameters: TParams, // TypeBox schema

  async execute(
    toolCallId: string,
    params: Static<TParams>,
    signal: AbortSignal | undefined,
    onUpdate: AgentToolUpdateCallback<TDetails> | undefined,
    ctx: ExtensionContext,
  ): Promise<AgentToolResult<TDetails>> {
    return {
      content: [{ type: "text", text: "result" }],
      details: {},
    };
  },
});
```

`name`, `label`, `description`, `parameters`, and `execute` are the core shape; prompt metadata, argument preparation, execution mode, and custom renderers are optional. The official example uses a TypeBox schema and returns `content` plus `details` ([Pi Extensions docs](https://pi.dev/docs/latest/extensions#quick-start)); the generic method and callback types are defined in Pi’s [official extension types](https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/src/core/extensions/types.ts).

